        <mxCell id="legend-planned" value="" style="rounded=1;absoluteArcSize=1;arcSize=6;fillColor=#64748b;fillStyle=hatch;hachureGap=9;hachureAngle=-41;fillWeight=1;dashed=1;dashPattern=6 4;strokeColor=#94a3b8;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="310" y="1644" width="40" height="18" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="legend-planned-text" value="&lt;span style=&quot;font-variant-ligatures:none&quot;&gt;planned · pill: target&lt;/span&gt;" style="text;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;fontFamily=JetBrains Mono,Noto Sans Mono,DejaVu Sans Mono,monospace;fontSize=10.5;fontColor=#e2e8f0;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="362" y="1642" width="188" height="22" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="card-legend-notes" value="&lt;span style=&quot;font-variant-ligatures:none&quot;&gt;Large dashed frame: infra perimeter · small: functional group&lt;br&gt;&lt;font color=&quot;#fb923c&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;⚠ Gx&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/font&gt;: docs and code disagree, see &quot;Gaps&quot;&lt;/span&gt;" style="text;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;whiteSpace=wrap;fontFamily=JetBrains Mono,Noto Sans Mono,DejaVu Sans Mono,monospace;fontSize=10.5;fontColor=#94a3b8;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="60" y="1700" width="480" height="40" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="card-status" value="&lt;span style=&quot;font-variant-ligatures:none&quot;&gt;&lt;font color=&quot;#fbbf24&quot;&gt;●&lt;/font&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;b&gt;&lt;font color=&quot;#f8fafc&quot; style=&quot;font-size:13px&quot;&gt;Where things stand&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;line-height:1.6&quot;&gt;• &lt;b&gt;&lt;font color=&quot;#f8fafc&quot;&gt;onprem&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/b&gt; is the only registered target, on the same K3s as the hub: tested end to end.&lt;br&gt;• &lt;b&gt;&lt;font color=&quot;#f8fafc&quot;&gt;&amp;lt;cloud-a&amp;gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/b&gt;: the aws and gcp cluster secrets exist but are left out of Argo CD until their Vault path is filled. Registering one is a one-line change.&lt;br&gt;• Each project record in cnp-projects carries &lt;b&gt;&lt;font color=&quot;#f8fafc&quot;&gt;target_cloud&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/b&gt;; Argo CD sends the project, prod and staging together, to that cluster.&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color:#f8fafc;color:#020617;border-radius:3px;padding:0px 4px;font-weight:bold;&quot;&gt;1&lt;/span&gt; to &lt;span style=&quot;background-color:#f8fafc;color:#020617;border-radius:3px;padding:0px 4px;font-weight:bold;&quot;&gt;5&lt;/span&gt;: user traffic enters through the project&amp;#39;s own tunnel on its cloud, never through on-prem (invariant I-1).&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;border:1px solid #f8fafc;color:#f8fafc;border-radius:3px;padding:0px 3px;font-weight:bold;&quot;&gt;A&lt;/span&gt; Argo CD syncs, &lt;span style=&quot;border:1px solid #f8fafc;color:#f8fafc;border-radius:3px;padding:0px 3px;font-weight:bold;&quot;&gt;B&lt;/span&gt; the secret operator reads Vault, &lt;span style=&quot;border:1px solid #f8fafc;color:#f8fafc;border-radius:3px;padding:0px 3px;font-weight:bold;&quot;&gt;C&lt;/span&gt; vmagent ships metrics: the only flows over the VPN, best effort.&lt;br&gt;• If on-prem is down, running apps keep serving and logging users in; nothing new deploys, no secret rotates.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/span&gt;" style="rounded=1;absoluteArcSize=1;arcSize=16;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;fillColor=#0b1222;strokeColor=#1e293b;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=20;spacingTop=14;spacingRight=16;fontFamily=JetBrains Mono,Noto Sans Mono,DejaVu Sans Mono,monospace;fontSize=11;fontColor=#e2e8f0;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="590" y="1460" width="900" height="290" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="card-gaps" value="&lt;span style=&quot;font-variant-ligatures:none&quot;&gt;&lt;font color=&quot;#fb923c&quot;&gt;●&lt;/font&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;b&gt;&lt;font color=&quot;#f8fafc&quot; style=&quot;font-size:13px&quot;&gt;Gaps between the plan and the code&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;line-height:1.6&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;font color=&quot;#fb923c&quot;&gt;G14&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/b&gt; &lt;b&gt;&lt;font color=&quot;#f8fafc&quot;&gt;Per-project edge.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/b&gt; Gateway, tunnel and Keycloak IAMaaS are in cnp-project-base, off by default. Live projects still use the hub&amp;#39;s shared gateway and tunnel.&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;font color=&quot;#fb923c&quot;&gt;G11&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/b&gt; &lt;b&gt;&lt;font color=&quot;#f8fafc&quot;&gt;Vault auth.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/b&gt; One Kubernetes auth mount for all clusters (D-07 not built).&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;font color=&quot;#fb923c&quot;&gt;G12&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/b&gt; &lt;b&gt;&lt;font color=&quot;#f8fafc&quot;&gt;Storage class.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/b&gt; local-path is hardcoded; no per-cloud profile (D-08).&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;font color=&quot;#fb923c&quot;&gt;G13&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/b&gt; &lt;b&gt;&lt;font color=&quot;#f8fafc&quot;&gt;Secret operator.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/b&gt; The Ricoberger operator, not HashiCorp VSO: whether a synced Secret survives a Vault outage is untested (GD-1).&lt;br&gt;• &lt;b&gt;&lt;font color=&quot;#f8fafc&quot;&gt;vmagent&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/b&gt; per cluster and the blackbox probes (D-10) are not started.&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;font color=&quot;#fb923c&quot;&gt;G3&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/b&gt; &lt;b&gt;&lt;font color=&quot;#f8fafc&quot;&gt;Transport.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/b&gt; TLS ends at Cloudflare; behind the tunnel, hops are plain HTTP.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/span&gt;" style="rounded=1;absoluteArcSize=1;arcSize=16;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;fillColor=#0b1222;strokeColor=#1e293b;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=20;spacingTop=14;spacingRight=16;fontFamily=JetBrains Mono,Noto Sans Mono,DejaVu Sans Mono,monospace;fontSize=11;fontColor=#e2e8f0;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1520" y="1460" width="980" height="290" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
</mxfile>
